    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_588c1e6e8514ee61385bddede089cedd6ab4cd74c20dd74095ed70e813b2722d",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: the span defines rho(x)=x-[x], chi as the indicator of (0,1], H=L2(0,infinity), rho_a(x)=rho(1/(ax)), B as the linear hull of the real-parameter family a>=1, and B^nat as generated by natural a; it then displays chi in B as the Nyman-Beurling criterion and announces chi in B^nat as the strengthening to be proved. Conditional interpretation: if the intended spaces are closed spans, the reformulation replaces zero location by Hilbert-space approximation and asks whether discretizing the dilation parameter preserves approximation power. Boundary: no closure mark or surrounding closure convention is visible, and this span contains neither an approximating sequence nor a proof.",
