    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_d878e5ea652c89c5b024c63b137290690d189cdcd56ffd3e1c3bbd236116008e",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: Corollary 3.1 makes RH equivalent to H-convergence of f_{epsilon,n} for every sufficiently small positive epsilon and describes the construction as a summability method. The source also asserts necessity and sufficiency along special subsequences, proposes studying a displayed Cesaro-smoothed Mobius sum, reports that a suitable epsilon might give an inverse-power-of-log-log-n error, and proposes an Lp extension. Interpretation: the established criterion and the proposed regularizations must be kept at different epistemic levels; the unused n-dependence in the Balazard-Saias lemma is offered as motivation for investigating the observed slowness, not as a rate theorem. Boundary: f_{epsilon,n}'s definition and the following proposition lie outside the unit.",
